@startuml
title Receiving a Pingback (synchronous)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Linking site" as Sender
participant "PingbackReceiverMiddleware\n/pingback.ping" as Middleware
participant "PingbackEndpoint" as Endpoint
participant "MentionReceiver" as Receiver
participant "Linking page\n(source)" as Source
database "tx_pongback_\ndomain_model_pingback" as Table
participant "NotifyEditors" as Mail

Sender -> Middleware : POST XML-RPC\npingback.ping(source, target)
Middleware -> Endpoint : handle()
Endpoint -> Endpoint : parse XML-RPC,\nrate limit per IP
Endpoint -> Receiver : receive(mention, site)
Receiver -> Receiver : target is a visible page\nof this site?
Receiver -> Table : already registered?
Receiver -> Source : GET source\n(public hosts only, max. 3 redirects, 1 MiB)
Source --> Receiver : HTML
Receiver -> Receiver : links to target?\ntitle and excerpt as plain text
Receiver -> Receiver : BeforePingbackCreateEvent\n(listeners may reject)
Receiver -> Table : store (hidden: waiting for approval)
Receiver -> Mail : AfterPingbackCreatedEvent
Mail -> Mail : email to\npongback.notification.emailTo
Receiver --> Endpoint : uid
Endpoint --> Sender : XML-RPC response "registered"

note over Endpoint, Receiver
  Any check failing ends here: the endpoint answers
  with the XML-RPC fault code of the specification,
  for example 17 (no link) or 48 (already registered).
end note
@enduml
